{
 "name": "Contraptions 19: Hilbert circuit, a soliton in every gate, gathering trap (Momentum Bubbles 17)",
 "description": "A Hilbert-curve circuit (order 3, 63 gates, each aiming at the next) at 512\u00b2: 63 dots (radius 3 cells) start at rest in every gate, which launch them along the curve into a trap on its last point (Momentum Bubbles 17), like a capacitor: a smooth round hill that brakes whatever comes in and draws it to its middle, senses how full it is, and once full (about 0.05 of it) lets go, sending what it collected straight east along the lowest row, round the frame into the first point, to go round again. Gates: brake, accel 0.002, aim_speed 0.025. Gates show as the aim channel, the trap as trap and full, in the custom palette. The trap feeds substrate and draws its catch to its middle, where the dots join into one blob; at about 3-5 dots it opens as a whole and launches the blob east round the frame into the first gate, then closes again.",
 "rule": "builtin:56",
 "size": 512,
 "start": "initial",
 "stepsPerFrame": 40,
 "globals": {
  "aim_speed": 0.025,
  "brake": 0.002,
  "accel": 0.002,
  "full_gain": 1000.0,
  "sense_rate": 0.001,
  "empty_at": 0.01,
  "sense_drain": 0.0,
  "full_at": 0.05
 },
